  "doc": "Typed event registry for the command center (PLAN.md §4, §7). The ingester validates every envelope against this file; anything that does not match is dead-lettered with a fixed code and raised as an unknown. Field spec keys (validated at load; any other key is a registry error): type (string, integer, number, boolean, array, object); required (default true); nullable (default false); enum or enum_ref; minimum and maximum (numbers); max_length (strings; default 256 for every string); code (true: 1-64 chars of A-Z, 0-9, _ . - only, for codes and identifiers, never free text); items (array element spec; object items declare fields). Undeclared fields are invalid. Envelope 'position' is the producer's immutable source position; the ingester verifies id == make_id(producer, position, type). 'seat_scoped' types must carry envelope 'seat' and are expected to carry 'agent' and 'binding' (missing ones raise U-identity). 'requires' lists envelope keys that must be non-null; 'requires_data' lists data keys that must be non-null and non-empty. Producers must be declared here (an undeclared producer is refused). max_tick_age_s: a producer whose last source.tick is older raises U-stale (I15); null means event-driven with no heartbeat bound. source.tick: position and complete_through_ms are required monotonic integers (byte offset or sequence; a time watermark); coverage is required and its counts must sum to records_emitted/ignored/quarantined by disposition (emitted, ignored, unknown); 'unavailable' marks a record type this host cannot read (an absent adapter): count 0, reason required, raises U-coverage adapter:<producer>/<runtime>/<record_type> until the type reports emitted or ignored. mail.sent@2 carries project_id (the Agent Mail project) and thread_root_id (nullable); with ack_required true it must carry request_id. request_id derivation (CC7:mail-contract; enforced by CC7:request-derivation, not by this registry): Agent Mail messages carry no request id, so every producer derives it deterministically as am-<project_id>-<thread_root_message_id>-<owner>, where thread_root_message_id is the message id of the first message of the thread and owner is the agent that owes the answer; equal inputs always give the same id (PLAN §8a requires an immutable id). mail.delivery@1 is one recipient's delivery receipt (envelope agent = data.recipient, else AGENT_RECIPIENT_MISMATCH). A message seen through several recipients' inboxes projects to one mail row (UNIQUE project_id, message_id) and one mail_deliveries row per recipient; a second mail.sent for the same message whose sender, recipients, importance, ack_required, request_id or thread_root_id differ raises U-conflict (same event key: SAME_KEY_DIFFERENT_PAYLOAD; different event key: MAIL_PAYLOAD_DRIFT). mail.ack@1 has no project_id, so mail_acks.project_id is resolved from the mail row when message_id names exactly one project, else NULL. service.state@1 is one kit job's status row; query_ok is required (a row without it is refused) so a failed service query is never mistaken for an unloaded job. service.health@2 adds generation (server run identity), dispatch_timeouts_total (nullable only when the server does not report it) and pool_utilization_pct (0..100, nullable). request.state follows opened -> answered|cancelled|moot. An integer is an I-JSON safe integer, -(2^53-1) to 2^53-1 inclusive (RFC 7493 §2.2): the range JavaScript holds exactly and a subset of SQLite's signed 64-bit range, so the TS spool (Number.isSafeInteger) and this ingester give one verdict on every integer (TICKNUM1). Envelope 'observed' is required: the future-time rule (U-clock) needs the producer's observation time.",
